@host = http://localhost:5280

### List bookmarks. Produces a three span trace: HTTP server, Bookmarks.List, postgresql.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks

### Create a bookmark. Ticks the bookmarks.created counter.
# @name create
POST {{host}}/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Distributed tracing primer",
  "url": "https://example.com/tracing",
  "description": "Saved for later",
  "kind": 1,
  "status": 1,
  "isArchived": false
}

### Read it back. Uses the id the create response returned.
@bookmarkId = {{create.response.body.id}}
GET {{host}}/bookmarks/{{bookmarkId}}

### Create a tag.
# @name createTag
POST {{host}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "observability",
  "description": "OpenTelemetry things"
}

### Attach the tag. Replaces the whole set, so this is all or nothing.
@tagId = {{createTag.response.body.id}}
PUT {{host}}/bookmarks/{{bookmarkId}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tagIds": ["{{tagId}}"]
}

### Replace the bookmark's fields.
PUT {{host}}/bookmarks/{{bookmarkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Distributed tracing, revised",
  "url": "https://example.com/tracing",
  "kind": 1,
  "status": 2,
  "isArchived": false
}

### Delete it.
DELETE {{host}}/bookmarks/{{bookmarkId}}

###
### Failure paths. Each one is a deliberate behaviour, not an accident.
###

### 400, and the message names the field you asked for. The reference returned 500 here.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks?sort=nonsense

### 400. Page size is capped at 100 so one request cannot read the whole table.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks?pageSize=1000

### 400. Page is one-based.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks?page=0

### 404, through the result type rather than a null return.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks/b_does_not_exist

### 409. Tag names are unique ignoring case, so this collides with "observability".
POST {{host}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Observability"
}

### 400, and the bookmark keeps the tags it already had. The upsert is all or nothing.
PUT {{host}}/bookmarks/{{bookmarkId}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tagIds": ["t_does_not_exist"]
}

### 406. The API serves JSON only.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks
Accept: application/xml

### Filtering, sorting and paging together.
GET {{host}}/bookmarks?q=tracing&kind=1&sort=title desc&page=1&pageSize=20
